<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.sensorium.unretires ~ a retirement reverses

`lares sense un-retire <name>` runs on a person's hand at a real terminal and returns a retired sensorium to its lifecycle; it asks no --approve.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ un-retire

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`un-retire` params=`name/pioneer-1 ~ restore a sensorium`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ name

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`name` params=`takes/name needs/required seat/1 as/<name> ~ the sensorium named in the manifest`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand ~ runs direct over manifest.json; a person at a real terminal, and the verb names its intent with --approve where it asks one`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ verb-error · hand-act-only

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`verb-error` params=`~ no name, or the un-retire refused`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`hand-act-only` params=`~ a seat reached a hand verb; name the command for the operator`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ restored

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`restored` params=`exit/0 ~ the manifest after`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

